# Netlify redirects. Preserve inbound links and published citations from the
# v1 /posts/ URL structure. v2 moved posts to /blog/<category>/<slug>/ AND
# changed some slugs, so each old URL needs an explicit 301 — a /posts/* splat
# would mis-map (the slugs differ, e.g. -across-pythia-model-sizes -> -pythia).

# Cited by Dung et al. (2026). This is the precursor article to the formal
# "Concept Emergence in the Pythia Suite" paper; the 301 resolves to the same
# article's current home (not the paper) so the citation lands on what was cited.
# Both trailing-slash variants listed so the exact cited URL (with slash) matches.
/posts/testing-accessibility-knowledge-across-pythia-model-sizes/   /blog/research/testing-accessibility-knowledge-pythia/   301
/posts/testing-accessibility-knowledge-across-pythia-model-sizes    /blog/research/testing-accessibility-knowledge-pythia/   301

